PS+=['Jack: Sweet heart! Why are you in a hurry?\nNina: Oh, please. Jack! Not now!\nJack: Where are you going?\nNina: (runs out of the house and jumps into the car) Talk to you later!!!\n(Two hours later)\nNina: J~A~C~K! Come pick up these big bags and heavy boxes! Mommy’s Help is having a big sale toady, and I went shopping there.\nJack: Oh my! Did you just move the entire store home?\nNina: Come on! We need all these things.\nJack: All right! Let me take a look. Five pairs of jeans? Seriously? Why do we need so many? And do you really think we need... 24 toothbrushes? 15 packs of cookies? And look at this! A coffee maker? Didn’t we just get one two months ago? And you don’t even love coffee!\nNina: Oh please! This one is different from the old one. It’s from Japan, and the salesperson told me that every family should have one...\nJack: Wait! A salesperson? Well, did he also tell you that this is the last one, and if you don’t buy it today, you will feel sorry later?\nNina: Yes!!! How did you know?\nJack: You are falling for the tricks of “hungry marketing.” Businesses often use it to make people suddenly feel the strong need to buy things. They will say something to make you feel bad for not buying. This way, they push you to spend money and at last get all the money in your pocket!\nNina: Oh no! Then what should I do?\nJack: Be a smart shopper! Don’t lose your mind and shop like crazy. Always look before you leap!\n\n(entire 整個的　coffee maker 咖啡機　suddenly 突然地)']
