PS+=['　　Clouds may look light and soft, but clouds are in fact not as light as they look. To find out how heavy a cloud is, we can’t just put it on a tool. We have to know its size and density.\n　　The picture below shows B’s density is higher than A’s. Different types of clouds have different densities. For example, cumulus clouds have a lot of water inside them. Another type is the cumulonimbus cloud. These clouds usually look darker and have a lot more water. Cirrus clouds are thin. We mostly see them on sunny days. The more water a cloud has, the higher density it has.\n（附圖：A、B 兩個方塊，B 內的小圓點比 A 多且密）\n　　Secondly, we can know the size of a cloud by driving a car across its shadow when the sun is right above it. After getting the size and density of a cloud, we can use math to know how heavy it is.\n　　It turns out that clouds are really heavy! A cumulus cloud is about 1.1 million pounds. It is like 100 elephants fly around above your head! Clouds are millions of small drops of water. The water in a cloud is not as heavy as the air around it. The air is much heavier, so it holds up the small drops of water. That’s why clouds can stay up in the sky.\n\n(soft 軟的　density 密度　shadow 影子)']
