PS+=['HNN News　10/21/2023\n　　Sean, a 14-year-old teenager, didn’t go to fast food restaurants or libraries to study like what his classmates usually did after school. He went straight home because his sick mother was waiting for him to look after her. Last year, his mother got seriously sick. His two high school sisters stopped going to school; they went to work to make money to pay for the medical cost. So, it’s Sean’s job to look after their mother. He didn’t know what to do with this big change in life.\n　　Teenagers like Sean are young carers. They are still young, but they need to have a strong mind. They can’t study or sleep well, and they can’t go out with friends. In other words, they don’t have their own young life. This also has bad effects on their life when they grow up. They may not do well at work or get along well with others.\n　　The young carers may lead to many problems, so the government should give help in time.\n（附圖：The number of young carers 長條圖，比較 USA、Australia、UK 三國）\n\n(medical 醫療的　young carer 年輕照顧者　government 政府)']
